{
  "question": "What is the largest sole-source award a federal agency can make to an SDVOSB for a requirement outside manufacturing?",
  "status": "answered",
  "answer": "Under federal rules, the largest sole-source award a contracting officer can make to an SDVOSB for a requirement outside manufacturing is $5 million. This limit applies when the anticipated award price, including options, does not exceed that amount for any NAICS code other than manufacturing. The rule is found in FAR 19.1406, which governs sole source awards to SDVOSB concerns.",
  "citations": [
